{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Is that why he was named?</b> It is an expression of astonishment, like 'Is this my brother?' — perhaps that is why his name was called Jacob, after what would happen at the end, that he would supplant me? Tanḥuma. Why did Isaac tremble? He said: perhaps there is sin in me, that I blessed the younger before the elder and altered the order of the birthright. Esau began to cry out, 'and he supplanted me these two times.' His father said to him, 'What did he do to you?' He said to him, 'He took my birthright.' He said, 'In that case I was distressed and trembling, lest perhaps I had transgressed the line of justice; now — the firstborn I have blessed; he shall indeed be blessed.'" "<b>And he supplanted me.</b> As the Targum renders and as Menachem — אֲרָבַנִי; and אָרַב — וּכְמַן. And there are those who translate וְחַכְמַנִי — he outwitted me." "<b>He withheld.</b> A term of setting aside, as in וַיָּאצֶל."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:49.742881321Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}